; /var/named/dynamic/ddns.myip.gr.hosts
;
; Minimal zone file for the RECOMMENDED dedicated DDNS zone (see README).
; Lives under /var/named/dynamic/ so named (-u named) can create the
; journal (.jnl) next to it — /var/named itself is not named-writable on EL.
;
; After loading, the zone is journal-managed: hand-edit only with
;   rndc freeze ddns.myip.gr  /  edit  /  rndc thaw ddns.myip.gr
; (You should rarely need to — goddns writes the records.)

$TTL 60
@   IN SOA  sdns.myip.gr. hostmaster.myip.gr. (
        1           ; serial (named bumps it via the journal)
        3600        ; refresh
        900         ; retry
        604800      ; expire
        60 )        ; negative-caching TTL

    IN NS   sdns.myip.gr.
; Add the other NS lines only if your slaves also carry this zone
; (then mirror allow-transfer/also-notify in named.conf). For TTL-60
; DDNS records, serving from the single master is usually fine:
;   IN NS   ns2.myip.gr.
;   IN NS   ns3.myip.gr.

; No A/AAAA records needed here — goddns creates them dynamically:
;   chris  IN A  <set by goddns>
;   vpn    IN A  <set by goddns>
